    "body": "This warrants more investigation to understand how different operating systems handle push/pop with report IDs. If push/pop changes how reports are interpreted it could be used to subvert protections based on the structure of the report descriptor. I think push/pop is extremely rare (I've never seen a device that uses push/pop), this increases the chance that the OS could interpret it differently than the browser.",
